# CLAUDE.md — {{projectName}}

This is a universal Expo SDK 57 application scaffolded by dude's
`expo-firebase` stack. It runs on Android, iOS, and web and uses the Firebase
JavaScript SDK for email/password Authentication and Cloud Firestore.

## Start here

```bash
dude cheatsheet --format json
dude doctor
```

## Layout

- `app/` contains thin Expo Router routes and auth guards.
- `src/features/` contains product behavior and screens.
- `src/components/` and `src/hooks/` contain reusable UI and hooks.
- `src/config/env.ts` is the only reader of `EXPO_PUBLIC_*` variables.
- `src/lib/firebase/` owns Firebase initialization and emulator wiring.
- `firestore.rules` and `tests/firestore.rules.test.mjs` are one security contract.

## Local development

Run `dude firebase emulators` in one terminal and `dude dev --go` in another.
The default `demo-` project cannot reach live Firebase resources. For a physical
device, follow `docs/docs/emulators.md` before exposing emulator ports to a
trusted LAN.

## Conventions

- Routes import feature screens; they do not call Firebase.
- Firestore access lives in `src/features/<feature>/repository.ts`.
- Auth access lives behind the auth feature service/provider.
- Shared code must remain platform-safe; browser-only code uses `.web.ts(x)`.
- Never weaken Firestore rules to make a client error disappear.
- Firebase public config identifies a project; rules authorize its data.
- Use pnpm. Do not edit `dude.json`, `.expo/`, `dist/`, or generated docs pages.

## Verification

```bash
dude lint
dude test
dude review
```

This stack intentionally has no security command group or native Firebase SDK.
Analytics, Crashlytics, Messaging, Functions, Storage, App Check, EAS Update,
and store submission are not part of this starter.
